324	
325	\paragraph{Anti-collapse regularizers.}
326	The regularizers we study, VICReg~\citep{bardes2022vicreg} and SIGReg~\citep{ball2025lejepa}, follow a line of work that includes Barlow Twins~\citep{zbontar2021barlowtwins} and W-MSE~\citep{ermolov2021whitening}. LeJEPA's characterization of the isotropic Gaussian as the optimal anti-collapse distribution provides the theoretical grounding for our tangent-space formulation. Neither VICReg nor SIGReg was originally studied with hyperbolic embeddings; the tangent-space variant we propose is, to our knowledge, new.
327	
328	\paragraph{Hyperbolic representation learning.}

